  "problem": "Express $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-1$ |  | $x+2$ |  | $2x-3$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+2}+\\frac{C}{2x-3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+10x-21=A(x+2)(2x-3)+B(x-1)(2x-3)+C(x-1)(x+2).\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+10(1)-21 & =A(1+2)(2(1)-3)+B(1-1)(2(1)-3)+C(1-1)(1+2) \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)^{2}+10(-2)-21 & =A(-2+2)(2(-2)-3)+B(-2-1)(2(-2)-3)+C(-2-1)(-2+2) \\\\ -21 & =21B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+10(\\frac{3}{2})-21 & =A(\\frac{3}{2}+2)(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(\\frac{3}{2}-1)(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+C(\\frac{3}{2}-1)(\\frac{3}{2}+2) \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{7}{4}C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{2}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{3}{2x-3}.\n$$",
